{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515584-sell-me-on-glory","id":515584,"title":"Sell me on Glory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-15T16:41:51-07:00","id":515584,"title":"Sell me on Glory","content":"With a lot of the Auspices I can picture pretty much exactly what they are supposed to be doing and their mechanics support this role. Rahu are giant blenders that murder everything in their wake. Full Moon gifts grant a bunch of combat buffs, and a lot of the Pure spirit gifts reinforce this with enough outliers that they aren't shoehorned <i>completely</i>. Irraka are ninja. They have gifts that help them ninja people in the kidneys and remain elusive/unseen. Ithaeur have the esoteric magic, information gathering and spirit angle covered. Their Gifts focus on taking down spirits, gathering information, and esoteric magic. Elodoth focus on finding and exploiting the truth / the Prey's support network and have the social angle largely covered. Their moon gift supports this, but their spirit gifts feel a bit all over the place.<br /> <br /> Then comes the Cahalith. In the fluff they are the storytellers and heralds. They rush in first and announce their prey's imminent destruction while bolstering their pack's moral with the stories they've collected. Okay, cool, I actually <i>really </i>like that. Then we turn to their gifts and... they're all over the place. Their Spirit Gifts while individually mostly okay, they don't collectively paint a picture of what the Cahalith is supposed to actually be <i>doing</i> on a hunt or to support their pack. They feel kind of like the pack Mario, a little good in everything without really excelling in anything. Their Pack buffs and mass debuffs (what I pictured them primarily doing) feel pretty underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Putting it in the context of a hunt...<br /> Against Werewolves<br /> <i>Rahu</i> fights everything.<br /> <i>Irraka</i> infiltrates and murders the key thing.<br /> <i>Ithaeur</i> gathers information and attacks their totem.<br /> <i>Elodeth</i> levies mortal influence, brokers deals between packs, and erodes their support network.<br /> <br /> Against Spirits<br /> <i>Rahu</i> fights everything it can.<br /> <i>Irraka</i> infiltrates and murders the key thing / delivers Bane directly to face.<br /> <i>Ithaeur</i> puts the spirit into a box the rest of his pack can actually affect.<br /> <i>Elodeth</i> manipulates essence through mortals, brokers deals with the spirit (courts) and damages cults.<br /> <br /> Against Humans<br /> <i>Rahu</i> fights everything.<br /> <i>Irraka</i> keeps the pack from getting caught.<br /> <i>Ithaeur</i> gathers information through spirit allies.<br /> <i>Elodeth</i> handles everything social.<br /> <br /> Against Ridden / Claimed<br /> Some combination of Humans and Spirits, depending on what exactly you are fighting.<br /> <br /> So what am I missing? Are the Cahalith better than they appear or am I completely off base with what they are supposed to be doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:28:46-07:00","id":515621,"title":"","content":"You seem to have a very decisive idea of what a pack should do, and I'd like to point out against a lot of their opponents, everyone will be fighting.<br /> <br /> That said, before the hunt the Cahalith gets dreams from Luna so they know what things she wants them to hunt. During the hunt, they make the hunt as epic as possible. After the hunt, they tell stories of the hunt to to give a reason for things like renown to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:02:20-07:00","id":515652,"title":"","content":"I'm referencing steriotypes and specialties. Practically speaking everyone will be doing a little of everything and characters are presumably multi-faceted and support each other in their specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T19:10:33-07:00","id":515686,"title":"","content":"If you were to break it down into military units:<br /> <br /> Rahu are the assault<br /> Elodoth are the tacticians <br /> Ithaeur are the intel<br /> Irraka are the special forces<br /> <br /> Cahalith are the support","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T19:14:55-07:00","id":515688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515584-sell-me-on-glory?p=515621#post515621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the hunt, they make the hunt as epic as possible. After the hunt, they tell stories of the hunt to to give a reason for things like renown to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appologize in advance for the number of f-bombs in this post. I mean no aggression or offense.<br /> I just looked back through the Glory-based Shadow Gifts. I saw three main threads which follow the Cahalith's stated role of &quot;know the story and tell it well&quot; pretty closely.<br /> <br /> 1) Know what's going on - Read the World's Loom was the best example of this, and it has great synergy with the Cahalith's in-born ability to have visions and know what's up before anyone else.<br /> <br /> 2) Inspire the Pack - This Story is True and Fearless Hunter go really well with the Glory-based Merit of Song in Your Heart to make Cahaliths an inspiration that keeps the pack driving hard. If you didn't perform the Moon's Mad Love Rite on the human elements of your Pack, Glorious Lunacy is a great inspirational tool, too!<br /> <br /> 3) Make it fucking awesome - Pretty much every other Glory Gift seemed like it was about going balls-to-the-wall. With Barghest, even if it's dead you can still kill it. With Catastrophe you unleash a fire-storm across at least two miles. With Fog of War you send the bullet from one enemy to the other. With Black Earth, Red Hunger you get to say &quot;and then the earth itself hungered for their blood. Vines and shoots cracked through the pavement and covered every inch of the alleyway, consuming their corpses in the process. No trace of them remained.&quot; With Unmake and a Glory of 3 (I imagine most Cahilith start at 2), you can stare down an oncoming pick-up truck, say &quot;Fuck you&quot; to it, and it will obligingly fall to pieces with the driver still going 65mph through the air. With Glory 5, you could do it to a tank and let the drivers get crushed by the rubble and exploding unspend munitions.<br /> <br /> Cahilith are all about the response. To them it matters more than the effect; if you can make your team go &quot;Fuck yeah!&quot; and your enemies go &quot;Holy shit!&quot;, you're 80% of the way there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 05-15-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T19:15:24-07:00","id":515689,"title":"","content":"Simply put, Cahalith motivate and support the pack. They provide history and experience through their stories. They provide inspiration and get the blood pumping with their songs. And they are fierce fighters and killers. Cahalith hold the pack together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T20:38:15-07:00","id":515729,"title":"","content":"The Cahalith puts it all together. They're the visionaries. The ones who understand the whole point of it all. You can do things well, yes, but <i>why</i> are you doing it? The Cahalith answers that question. When you have an &quot;Oh, shit,&quot; moment and realize that what you've been working towards is actually a piece of a much, much larger puzzle and if you pick wrong, you might fuck everything up? You don't turn to your Elodoth or your Ithaeur; you turn to your Cahalith. When you're shell-shocked by what's happening around you, who talks you through it? The Cahalith. How do you know you're doing the right thing? Because your Cahalith is backing you up, or leading the charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T22:12:55-07:00","id":515829,"title":"","content":"Rahu: Fighter<br /> Ithaeur: Mage<br /> Elodoth: Cleric<br /> Irraka: Rogue<br /> Cahalith: Bard","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T22:05:06-07:00","id":517646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515584-sell-me-on-glory?p=515829#post515829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rahu: Fighter<br /> Ithaeur: Mage<br /> Elodoth: Cleric<br /> Irraka: Rogue<br /> Cahalith: Bard</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. Like the D&amp;D bard, many people have trouble seeing what a Cahalith can contribute to the group. To them, I would reply with <a href=\"https://uproxx.files.wordpress.com/2015/05/mad-max-guitarist.jpg?w=650&amp;h=435\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T02:41:27-07:00","id":517787,"title":"","content":"When you're looking at the auspice roles it sometimes pays to look to the tribe that shares their favoured renown. In the Cahalith's case, this is the Blood Talons, also known as Camp Murder Shit. And the Gibbous Moon gift bears this out somewhat. Four of the five facets are about giving them the edge in a fight. The difference is that they benefit the whole pack rather than just the Cahalith because they focus on making the prey weaker instead of making the werewolf stronger.<br /> <br /> With the exception of War Howl which is 100% bard move. <i>&quot;Murder, murder, murder the foe; With your Teeth and Claws&quot;. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T08:38:52-07:00","id":518092,"title":"","content":"I see the Cahalith as being research experts. They're not just meant to tell the stories of the Pack's exploits, but learn and share the stories of other packs stories. This helps provide important information such as tactics, personalities, how people could respond when the pack learns they need to deal with particular parties. <br /> <br /> The focus on learning stories also extends to delving into the histories of a location and spirits to learn important details. The lore of a region that a Cahalith can dig up can help pinpoint where important loci could be (and help the Irraka get where they need to be to actually find it). The Cahalith helps learn lore for the Itheaur to construct effective rituals or find appropriate offerings to appease spirits or powerful weapons in a spirits ban or bane. The Cahalith similarly helps the Elodoth with the research and person skills. Finally, the Cahalith can stand as a powerful combatant that can support and strengthen the Rahu.<br /> <br /> Everyone in the pack has a role. Each of the other auspices have important individual goals, and it can be hard to see where the Cahalith fits precisely, but that's because they don't. The Cahalith is woven to interact with each of those roles, providing support, intelligence and foresight to make the individuals in those roles even more effective. <br /> <br /> The Cahalith is a pillar than upholds the pack, makes it stronger, makes it able to withstand all sorts of blows and at the end of the day, keeps the pack focused on what they can and could accomplish so they stay unbowed and unbroken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T05:08:58-07:00","id":519433,"title":"","content":"Having just read &quot;a rumour of war&quot; it occurs to me that a platoon's seemingly invincible, terrifying lead NCO very much seems like a Cahalith archetype. They carry the mythology of the marine corps, they bully, cajole, support and defend the ranks in order to make them into an effective, aggressive force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:16:01-07:00","id":519651,"title":"","content":"I pretty much just play Cahalith, so I'll add my insight. The Cahalith exists to push the pack to excel in every way, and then tell the stories of how badass the pack is. You push the pack to be the strongest, most powerful pack they can be, with things like <b>Fearless Hunter</b>and <b>The Pack Triumphs Together</b>. You tell the war stories, the hunting tales to the pups, so they do better; <b>This Story is True</b> and <b>Know Thy Prey</b>. When a different pack enters your territory, a Cahalith steps up and howls out the savage, mighty deeds of the pack, daring the intruders to act; <b>War Howl</b> and <b>Voice of Glory.</b><br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Cahalith can stand on their own, and operate without the Pack at their back. Prey will have no respite, can find no friend, and stop the Cahalith; <b>Dream Hunter, Know Thy Prey </b>and <b>Fearless Hunter</b>. A Cahalith is informed, persuasive, and can deny their prey those advantages,<b> Needle, Sift the Sand</b>, <b>Know thy Prey, </b>and <b>Voice of Glory.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:21:19-07:00","id":519681,"title":"","content":"Nice to hear the side of someone who primarily plays them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:29:11-07:00","id":519687,"title":"","content":"I never get to play Alpha, so I'm happy playing second fiddle which may color my opinion. In my current pack, the alpha is a former gang member turned security guard, who loves the phrase &quot;If you don't like it, leave&quot;. My Cahalith Iron Master turns his sandpaper attitude into clear plans and &quot;gentle&quot; urgings, while at the same time laying into the alpha about control and phrasing. A cahalith is the glue that keeps the pack from pulling apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:23:15-07:00","id":521773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/515584-sell-me-on-glory?p=519651#post519651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, a Cahalith can stand on their own, and operate without the Pack at their back.[/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Cahailith are great for one player one gm stories.<br /> They are fantastic in a pack, but they are just as good without one around them. Great for a small pack with few uratha.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:11:20-07:00","id":527077,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, everyone! Wound up making a 20-EXP 2 Glory, 2 Honor, 1 Wisdom, highly social Cahalith / Bone Shadow. The other two werewolf members of the pack wound up being a highly physical Cunning / Purity Irraka Hunter in Darkness and a highly mental Wisdom / Cunning Iron Master, which was a nice bit of accidental complimentary character building. My Gifts and Facets are: Gibbous Moon 2; (Insight) Read the World's Loom, One Step Ahead; (Knowledge) This Story is True, Know Thy Prey; (Pack) Pack Awareness. Notably I took almost every Tribe and Reknown-based merit I qualified for (Song of Your Heart, Warcry, Shadow Whispers, Impartial Mediator). Looking at it objectively, with this set-up being Glory / Cahalith gets me...<br /> <br /> The ability to...<br /> - have Prophetic Dreams (Under ST Control)<br /> - pass out a +3 bonus or turn an action into a failure for a beat 1/session.<br /> - ask questions about the future. - inflict a Persistent Inspired condition on my allies (beat machine for them and some social manipulation possible).<br /> - inflict -1 to Defense and Attack Rolls as well as -2 to Initiative to a small group of enemies.<br /> - grant my allies +1L damage to all attacks for a small number of turns.<br /> - grant my allies or myself bonus to a particular skill for the rest of the scene (only skills rated at 0, 1 or 2).<br /> - gain +(Glory) [2] to Expression and Persuasion rolls for a scene as well as increase impression level (my group sadly almost never uses social maneuvering).<br /> <br /> Can't really fight well outside of Garou. I like how the concept turned out either way, a Graffiti Artist who uses their Art (capital A) to mark territory, do rites, tell stories, influence his community and shepherd spirits. Uses the &quot;downside&quot; of Warcry after making a good piece of art to call all nearby curious spirits and then go, &quot;Hey, look at this Art I made&quot; and Inspiration quality on an exceptional success to cultivate particular emotions/actions. Decided to turn my hesitation with regards to this guy being useful on the Hunt into a long-term Aspiration, &quot;Prove my worth on the Hunt.&quot; In the meantime, he'll be rather excellent at information gathering and has some social sledgehammers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}